THE HIGH ELVIS\'92S VOICE \'97 the technique, in full\

\f2 \uc0\u9642 
\f0  The register: the voice BOOMS \'93despite sinking into the tired furnishings.\'94 The room absorbs him and he carries anyway.\

\f2 \uc0\u9642 
\f0  The method: sentences built out of Elvis song titles and lyrics, threaded so densely that the seams disappear. The spec\'92s first inauguration runs, in order: all shook up \'b7 my hands are shaking and my knees are weak \'b7 a fool such as I \'b7 pocket full of rainbows \'b7 burning love \'b7 suspicious minds \'b7 big boss man \'b7 always on my mind \'b7 I love you so \'b7 long Jericho road \'b7 cross my heart and hope to die \'b7 make the morning \'b7 you\'92ll never walk alone \'b7 a little less conversation and a little more action \'b7 washed my hands in muddy waters \'b7 it is no secret \'b7 it\'92s a wonderful world \'b7 you\'92re the reason I\'92m living \'b7 give me all of your love \'b7 I\'92ll never stand in your way \'b7 peace in the valley \'b7 pledging my love \'b7 let me be the one \'b7 only the strong survive \'b7 please don\'92t stop loving me.\

\f2 \uc0\u9642 
\f0  The drafted new High Elvis uses the same technique at about a third the density and in a mournful key (promised land, crying in the ghetto, wooden heart, it\'92s now or never, there goes my everything, separate ways, if I can dream, only the strong survive). THE RUNNING ORDER WANTS HIS SPEECH TO ECHO THE FIRST \'97 this list is what there is to echo.\

